The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
for (i = 0; i < PTE_PREFETCH_NUM; i++, spte++) {
    if (is_shadow_present_pte(*spte) || spte == sptep) {
        if (!start)
            continue;
        if (direct_pte_prefetch_many(vcpu, sp, start, spte) < 0)
            break;
        start = NULL;
    } else if (!start)
        start = spte;
}
```
Reason:
The loop iterates over the SPTEs, but if all preceding SPTEs are not present, it fails to prefetch any trailing SPTEs that follow the faulting GFN. This results in the loop terminating without handling these trailing SPTEs, leading to an increased number of guest page faults.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
+	if (start)
+		direct_pte_prefetch_many(vcpu, sp, start, spte);
```
Reason:
This addition ensures that after the loop, if there are any trailing SPTEs that need to be prefetched (indicated by `start` being non-null), a final call to `direct_pte_prefetch_many()` is made. This effectively handles the previously missed trailing SPTEs, reducing the number of guest page faults.

